<title>USA: Farm Credit Systems Q1 net interest income falls.</title>
<headline>Farm Credit Systems Q1 net interest income falls.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter Ended March 31,</p>
<p>						 1997	  1996</p>
<p>Interest income			  $1,433     $1,450</p>
<p>Interest expense			   (900)	(895)</p>
<p>Net interest income			 533	  555</p>
<p>Provision for loan losses		 (40)	 (18)</p>
<p>Net noninterest expenses		 (146)	(140)</p>
<p>Income before income taxes		347	  397</p>
<p>Provision for income taxes		(44)	 (43)</p>
<p>Net income				 $  303     $  354</p>
<p>				(Data in Millions)</p>
<p>NOTE: Farm Credit Systems reported total assets for the first quarter of 1997 were $75.3 billion, compared with $74.9 billion for the quarter ended December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>Farm Credit Systems is a nationwide system of federally chartered agricultural and rural lending institutions cooperatively owned by their borrowers.</p>
</text>
